Slide 2 — THE PROBLEM

AML generates alerts. The real challenge is resolving them.

Banks already monitor millions of transactions.
But sophisticated financial crime can hide across patterns, relationships and multiple hops.

What gets missed?

ISOLATED TRANSACTIONS
A suspicious transaction can look normal on its own.

HIDDEN NETWORKS
Layering, mule accounts and circular movement span multiple accounts.

EVOLVING PATTERNS
New typologies can emerge faster than static rules are updated.

INVESTIGATION OVERLOAD
Thousands of alerts still require analysts to manually connect the dots.

THE GAP

Detection without context creates alerts.
Investigation without intelligence creates workload.

